.TH TGLFS-SYNC 1 "May 2026" "tglfs 0.1.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tglfs-sync \- back up and restore local folders with TGLFS sync manifests
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tglfs sync init
\fIfolder\fR \fB--name\fR \fIname\fR
.br
.B tglfs sync push
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fIfolder-or-root-id\fR
.br
.B tglfs sync pull
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fIroot-id\fR \fIdestination\fR
.br
.B tglfs sync status
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fIfolder-or-root-id\fR
.br
.B tglfs sync list
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B sync
command group implements the first TGLFS folder-sync milestone: backup and restore. It stores one
.B tglfs:sync-manifest
record per sync root in Telegram Saved Messages. File contents remain ordinary immutable
.B tglfs:file
records; the manifest maps normalized relative paths to UFIDs and file metadata.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B init <folder> --name <name>
Create a local sync-root ledger entry and publish an empty remote manifest.
.TP
.B push <folder-or-root-id>
Scan the configured local folder, upload new or changed files, mark deleted paths as tombstones, and publish the updated manifest after uploads complete.
.TP
.B pull <root-id> <destination>
Restore non-deleted manifest entries into the destination folder. Existing divergent files are preserved by writing the remote file to a deterministic conflict path.
.TP
.B status <folder-or-root-id>
Compare the configured local folder against the remote manifest and print added, modified, deleted, and unchanged counts.
.TP
.B list
List locally configured sync roots.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --no-interactive
Disable interactive prompts and fail instead of prompting.
.TP
.B --password <password>
Encryption password for
.B push
or decryption password for
.B pull.
.TP
.B --password-env [name]
Read the sync password from an environment variable. If no name is provided, the command uses
.B TGLFS_SYNC_PASSWORD.
.TP
.B --password-stdin
Read the sync password from standard input.
.TP
.B --json
Emit machine-readable JSON.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B TGLFS_SYNC_PASSWORD
Default environment variable for sync upload and restore passwords.
.SH FILES
Sync roots are stored in the CLI data directory in
.B sync-roots.json.
.SH AI AGENT NOTES
This sync milestone is backup/restore only. It does not install a daemon, watch the filesystem, or provide a GUI. Do not overwrite conflicts: preserve both files and report the conflict path.
